Platform is up, and billing. Two commands left:

  1. Build the stack's images and import them into every node:

       cd ../.. && ./build.sh ubuntu@<public-ip> ubuntu@<public-ip> ubuntu@<public-ip> ubuntu@<public-ip> ubuntu@<public-ip> 

  2. Apply the workload:

       KUBECONFIG=cloud/aws/./kubeconfig.yaml kubectl apply -k manifests/

  Then the tunnel, unchanged from Hetzner (GOTCHAS.md item 13: it has to land
  on the node running the console pod):

       ssh -i /Users/yukos/.ssh/stack-k8s-aws -L 17420:$(kubectl -n agent-stack get svc genaryx-console -o jsonpath='{.spec.clusterIP}'):7420 ubuntu@<node running the console>

  A public entry point is a separate, metered decision: manifests/50-loadbalancer.yaml,
  and on AWS it is an NLB at USD 0.027/hour plus capacity units.

  When done: ./teardown.sh  (the hourly figure terraform apply printed says so)

