A call with no key, or one the gateway does not hold, is refused 401, and the key
speaking as an id outside agents/ is refused 403 identity_mismatch. To read it
again on another machine: kubectl -n agent-stack get secret gateway-client-keys -o jsonpath='{.data.client_keys}' | base64 --decode
(the entry ending :agents). To give each agent its own key and unit, run
identity/up.sh with a keys file and an identity map, both together.
